1. Super Admin Setup
What happens:
Platform owner logs in
Creates:
School
Default Academic Year
Why it matters:

This enables multi-tenant architecture (your ERP can serve multiple schools)

🏫 2. School Creation Flow
Steps:
Enter school details
Generate unique school code
Assign primary admin
Real-world example:

A trust managing 5 schools registers each branch under one umbrella

🏢 3. Branch Setup
Steps:
Add multiple branches/campuses
Assign branch admins
Scenario:

Main campus + junior campus + hostel campus

📆 4. Academic Year Initialization
Steps:
Define academic year (2025–26)
Set active year
Why critical:

All operations (fees, attendance, exams) are tied to this

🏫 5. Class & Section Configuration
Steps:
Create classes (Grade 1–10)
Add sections (A, B, C)
Real-world nuance:

Different branches may have different class structures

👤 6. User Onboarding (Admin Level)
Steps:
Create School Admin
Assign role
Map to school/branch
Output:

Login credentials generated

🔐 7. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
Capabilities:
Super Admin → Full control
School Admin → Limited to their school
Teacher → Academic-only access
⚙️ 8. System Configuration
Examples:
Timezone
Currency
Default grading system